### Public menu (also usable as an Insomnia GET request)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/restaurant/menu/?ordering=price

### Register using YOUR OWN local test credentials
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/auth/users/
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"reviewer","email":"reviewer@example.test","password":"REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_STRONG_PASSWORD","re_password":"REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_STRONG_PASSWORD"}

### Obtain a token, then copy auth_token to protected requests
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/auth/token/login/
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"reviewer","password":"REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_STRONG_PASSWORD"}

### Create a reservation
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/restaurant/booking/tables/
Authorization: Token REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Ada","no_of_guests":2,"booking_date":"2030-01-01T18:00:00Z"}

### List your reservations
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/restaurant/booking/tables/
Authorization: Token REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_TOKEN

### Update your own reservation (replace id with response id)
PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/restaurant/booking/tables/1/
Authorization: Token REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{"no_of_guests":4}

### Delete your own reservation
DELETE http://127.0.0.1:8000/restaurant/booking/tables/1/
Authorization: Token REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_TOKEN

### Create a dish with a staff token
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/restaurant/menu/
Authorization: Token REPLACE_WITH_STAFF_TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{"title":"Lemon pasta","price":"12.50","inventory":20}
